  <h3 style="margin-top:26px">Indexed collections</h3>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:14px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Collection</th><th>What it settled</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="https://www.familysearch.org/search/collection/1974196">Argentina, Santa Fe,
          Catholic Church Records, 1634–2003</a></td>
          <td>No Lerena marriage at Rosario 1868–1891; the first Lerenas in the city, at Santa Rosa de
            Lima, 1903 and 1918</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Argentina, National Census, <strong>1869</strong> and <strong>1895</strong></td>
          <td>Bartolomé Llerena in Rosario in 1869; no Lerena in Santa Fe in 1895</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Argentina, Baptisms, 1645–1930</td>
          <td><strong>Two</strong> Lerena baptisms in the whole indexed country</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Uruguay, Civil Registration 1879–2020 · Catholic Church Records 1726–2000 ·
          Baptisms 1750–1900</td>
          <td>The Trinidad, Montevideo and Colonia kindreds — and no Pablo Armando in any of them</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Argentina, Entre Ríos, Civil Registration, 1833–1965</td>
          <td>The four-generation Larena family at Gualeguaychú</td></tr>
